{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 964,
    "dDurationMs": 2216,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have known for a long time that the universe is expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3180,
    "dDurationMs": 2555,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at distant galaxies, they are moving away from us,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5735,
    "dDurationMs": 3335,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the more distant galaxies are moving faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9070,
    "dDurationMs": 2976,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So really, it’s not really an explosion of galaxies away from us;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12046,
    "dDurationMs": 3073,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All galaxies are moving away from all the other galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15119,
    "dDurationMs": 3265,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Space itself is getting bigger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18384,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you would expect that the expansion of the universe is something that will slow down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22017,
    "dDurationMs": 3287,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These galaxies have gravity and they attract each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25304,
    "dDurationMs": 2894,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you would expect that the expansion of the universe will diminish with time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28198,
    "dDurationMs": 4919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it was a big surprise in 1998 when we realized that the galaxies were actually speeding up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33117,
    "dDurationMs": 2737,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you look at one galaxy, non-only it is moving away from us,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35854,
    "dDurationMs": 2928,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But tomorrow it will be moving away from us faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38782,
    "dDurationMs": 2654,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what we call the acceleration of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41436,
    "dDurationMs": 2032,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we are not completely shocked,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43468,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a good theoretical model handed down to us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46098,
    "dDurationMs": 1707,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Einstein."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47805,
    "dDurationMs": 4862,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea that even empty space has energy, what we call vacuum energy or dark energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52667,
    "dDurationMs": 5679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this vacuum energy pushes space itself and causes distant galaxies to move away from us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58346,
    "dDurationMs": 3887,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Faster and faster. That is where the acceleration comes from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62233,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So theoretical cosmologists are trying to understand what could be going on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65766,
    "dDurationMs": 3323,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is it really vacuum energy? Is some variation of that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69089,
    "dDurationMs": 4243,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or is it even a modification of Einstein’s general relativity, our theory of gravity?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73332,
    "dDurationMs": 3699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If vacuum energy is the right answer, the universe will continue to expand,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77031,
    "dDurationMs": 4568,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The galaxies will move away from us and the universe will gradually become a lonelier, darker,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81599,
    "dDurationMs": 359917401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "emptier place."
    } ]
  } ]
}
